Supply the ADMIN password first — 12-30 characters, set in the same shell that
runs `terraform`. The variable is ephemeral, so the value never reaches a file,
a plan or state. The value is **just the password**:

```bash
# macOS / Linux (zsh, bash) — single quotes, so $ ! # in the password are kept
export TF_VAR_aws_adb_admin_password='YourPassword12'
```

```powershell
# Windows PowerShell — `export` does nothing here
$env:TF_VAR_aws_adb_admin_password = 'YourPassword12'
```

It applies to every database using `admin_password_source = "write_only"`. To
give {% if wo | length > 1 %}them different passwords{% else %}a database its own password{% endif %}, use the map instead — there the
value is HCL, so the inner double quotes are required:

```bash
export TF_VAR_aws_adb_admin_passwords='{ {% for a in wo %}{{ a.module_name }} = "..."{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} }'
```

A password containing a single quote: in bash/zsh write it as `'\''`; in
PowerShell double it (`''`). If no password is found, the plan stops and says so.
